-- ── hand-written: who may read and write the log ────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- A member sees the emails of the documents they can see: the policy asks the sales documents'
-- own policy, so a salesperson sees the emails of their own documents and a member limited to
-- some branches those branches' only. A member who may write sales documents may email one that
-- has its number, as themselves, now, starting as "sending". Afterwards only the outcome columns
-- can change, only while the outcome is not yet known, and the outcome is written now, by the
-- member writing it. Nothing is ever deleted by the app.
--
-- The times are the database's own: a "sending" row dated in the future would look as if it were
-- still being sent, for ever, and stop the document being emailed again.
REVOKE ALL ON public.sales_document_emails FROM anon, authenticated;
